<title>ROMANIA: ROMANIA NET AVERAGE WAGE 2.8 PCT UP IN AUGUST.</title>
<headline>ROMANIA NET AVERAGE WAGE 2.8 PCT UP IN AUGUST.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average net wage in</p>
<p>Romania went up 2.8 percent in August from July, a rise below a</p>
<p>3.8 percent monthly inflation, National Statistics Board (CNS)</p>
<p>data showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p> ROMANIAN AVERAGE WAGES   AUG 96     JULY 96	 AUG 95</p>
<p> monthly change	     +2.8	  +13.5	   +5.4</p>
<p> yr/yr change		+49.0	  +52.7	  +49.7</p>
<p> wage in ROL	     343,090	333,797	230,338</p>
<p>NOTE: The CNS said purchasing power slipped by 1.0 percent in</p>
<p>August from July but was 3.3 percent up year-on-year. It said</p>
<p>August's purchasing power was 73.1 percent of the 1990 level.</p>
<p>Employees in the banking sector had the highest net wage of</p>
<p>659,122 lei on average in August when workers in the health and</p>
<p>social security sectors had the lowest pay -- 251,391 lei.</p>
<p>Romania employed 5.826 million people at end-August, 49,300</p>
<p>less than the previous month.</p>
<p>-- Mirela Eremia, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
</text>
